WEBVTT

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:19.360
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:19.360
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:19.360
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:46.160
Silver-White Valley

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:46.160
Chapter 3

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:54.640
In July of Space Year 791,
Imperial Year 482...

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.650
...a battle between the Galactic
Empire and Free Planets Alliance...

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:03.310
...was to add a page to the history of seemingly endless warfare...

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:07.210
...taking place in one corner of this
frontier planet, Kapche-Lanka.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.530
Be careful.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.890
It looks like there's more
than one enemy unit here.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:01.300
If we spread out, we'll get
annihilated one by one.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.510
Let's stay together.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.610
Let's position ourselves with that cliff behind us.
That way, it'll be easier to watch out for attacks.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:59.610
Because the first battle for Reinhard
von Musel and Siegfried Kircheis...

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:02.060
...took place on a world
below the freezing point...

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:04.340
...it was eerily
inorganic and surreal.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.590
There was no smell of
blood or warmth of flesh.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:11.090
For that reason, there was little
sense of bloodshed in the killing.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.420
It may have been an extreme
of one facet of warfare...

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:18.800
...where human beings are viewed as
expendable supplies, reducible to numbers.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:24.000
It's no good.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.530
The controls seem to depend on
direct input from this driver-helmet...

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:30.310
...which is directly connected to
the vehicle's artificial intelligence.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.140
But the pattern of brainwaves
seems to be specified...

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:37.210
...so it appears that only those who
are already registered can access it.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.860
In that case, we can't seize
the armored vehicle itself.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:43.110
That's right.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.720
Unlike those of the Imperial Forces, it
doesn't seem that we can control it manually.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:50.860
Then we should at least
take the fuel and data.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:52.920
Is the hydrogen
battery interchangeable ?

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:53.890
Yes.

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:55.920
We can probably do it if we
connect the line directly to it.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:15.640
Lieutenant.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.910
I want you to go
and follow them now.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.170
What ?

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.510
Well, unless I see proof...

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.810
"...you don't feel safe" ?

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:29.660
Well, I have to
send a report, too.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.610
Besides, if the unlikely were
to happen, it'll be trouble.

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:33.790
If the unlikely were
to happen, you say.

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:36.050
If that happens,
what shall we do ?

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:37.870
It goes without saying.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:41.970
Understood, sir.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:00.960
It's connected.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:01.760
Please try it.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.040
Okay.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.380
It's working.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:10.160
Yes.

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:14.050
Now, if we can get data from this file to
determine the location of the enemy base...

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:16.170
...our first mission
will be perfect.

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:18.960
But before that, we should
get something to eat.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.880
After all, we can use
the cooking devices now.

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:22.270
Sure.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:32.210
I wonder if this
is the end of it.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:34.290
You mean ?

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:37.950
Criminals always return to the
scene of the crime for confirmation.

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:41.150
Whether it's the Captain himself or
someone ordered by the Captain...

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:44.970
...someone will come
to confirm our deaths.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:46.620
Don't you agree ?

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.660
I see.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:49.310
You're right.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:50.660
What are we going to do ?

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.970
Oh, you're alive ?

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:30.120
You're very lucky.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:31.380
Lieutenant !

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:32.460
You came to rescue us !

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:36.530
Ensign, what happened
to your subordinate ?

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:38.900
I don't see
that red-haired guy.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:41.490
Well...

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:46.150
...since we ran out of fuel, we couldn't move
the vehicle or we couldn't use our weapons.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:50.790
He went to call for help,
and he fell into the valley.

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:52.080
I couldn't save him...

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.840
Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:56.900
I want to look
for his body.

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:58.070
Please give me a hand.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:02.040
After that, I'd like to get in your
vehicle and go back to the base.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:04.250
I'm sorry, but you can't.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:07.470
I didn't come to
rescue you, after all.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:08.290
What ?

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:10.160
Then why did
you come here ?

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:13.410
It's no use keeping
it a secret now.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:18.200
I came to keep you from coming
back to the base ever again, Ensign.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.700
So I followed your
radio transmitter.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.790
But of course, I was hoping you had
already died from the cold or in battle.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:30.010
But I guess I have to do some
physical labor from time to time.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:30.750
What ?

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:35.340
For you, your first
battle will be your last.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:40.120
It's quite unfortunate,
but it's not at all a rarity.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:44.160
After all, the first battle
is the most difficult one.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:45.460
Give it up.

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:49.000
Just follow after your
red-haired comrade.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:52.700
If Captain Herder finds out,
you won't go unpunished.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:57.960
Captain Herder gave the order
to kill you in the first place.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:09:59.170
What ?!

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:00.450
Why ?!

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:01.920
What did I do ?!

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:04.890
I don't remember having done
anything to offend the Captain !

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:08.450
Just the fact that
you're here offends us.

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:11.770
I'm Countess Grunewald's brother !

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:14.920
That means I'll
soon be your superior.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:17.530
You think you'll go unpunished
if you do things like this ?

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:20.850
So your arrogance comes
from your sister's power ?

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:22.580
But how unfortunate...

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.820
...something like that
will soon cease to exist.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:30.150
After all, the source of that light
itself will soon be extinguished.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:31.520
What ?

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:37.720
Captain Herder is connected
to some noble person at Court.

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:41.620
About the time you two
arrived on this planet...

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.880
...he received a secret
letter from that certain person.

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:49.110
This person is a lady much
favored by His Majesty.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:56.760
She says she won't allow some wench from
a poor aristocratic family to rule at Court.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:01.220
And as a matter of course,
she wants the brother to be killed.

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:04.360
Who is this lady ?

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:09.560
Since you won't live to
tell anyone, I'll tell you.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:10.660
Her name is...

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:15.200
...Marquise Benemunde.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.120
I've heard of her.

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:21.820
She's the lady whom His Majesty
favored before my sister.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:23.580
That's right.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.700
She's a born lady.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:29.020
Much nobler than a
slut like your sister !

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:40.100
Okay then.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:42.170
I have no more use for you.

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:44.440
Kircheis, do it !

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:48.630
What ?

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:03.780
Oh ?

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:04.760
You're still alive ?

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:11.590
Please save me...

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:14.440
Please...

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:17.170
If you save me...

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:21.220
I will be loyal to you...

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:23.270
What shall we do, Kircheis ?

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:27.680
This man insulted
Lady Annerose...

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.420
...and desecrated her name.

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:36.210
Did you hear that, Lieutenant ?

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:38.840
I agree with him.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.060
I can forgive you
for trying to kill us.

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.960
After all, it was a matter
of your position as well.

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:46.640
But you said something you
should have never said.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.240
There's no other way
to atone for your sin.

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:07.130
To think we have to fight
against these pieces of scum.

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:13.450
Let's head back to base, Kircheis.

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:14.630
It's only the
beginning of our battle.

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:16.580
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:20.540
That's right.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:21.960
Our battle has only begun.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:25.860
We must exact an appropriate
retribution from Captain Herder...

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:31.500
...and protect Lady Annerose from the plots of the Court aristocrats who are pulling his strings.

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:37.750
That might temporarily strengthen the ties
between Lady Annerose and the Kaiser.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:42.400
But as long as
we're all alive...

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:50.270
As long as we're all alive, I believe, someday, she'll smile for me.

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:55.270
With that belief,
I will fight.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:56.350
For now.

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:40.520
Lord Reinhard, here it is.

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:42.470
This is the data
on the enemy base.

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:43.330
Good.

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:49.290
And the enemy operation
plans as well.

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:53.320
It seems they're heading
toward our base right now.

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:55.510
What ?

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:57.910
At this rate, there'll be a
surprise attack on our base.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:01.710
It seems that the enemy unit we
encountered wasn't just on routine patrol...

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:04.120
...they were an advance scout unit.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:07.680
Lord Reinhard ?

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:11.570
I wonder if there's a way to
take advantage of this situation ?

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:29.660
...respond !

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.210
Guard post #12, respond !

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:32.560
Guard post #3, respond !

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:34.080
Guard post #8, respond !

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:34.080
What's going on ?

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:36.580
It's a surprise attack.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:40.500
Communications with guard posts #3, #8,
and #12 were cut off at nearly the same time.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:43.380
At a time like this ?

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.120
Yes ?

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:47.600
I...it's nothing.

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:49.920
Order level one
defensive measures.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:50.940
Yes, sir.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:52.680
Level one defensive measures !

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:57.380
We've detected multiple launches by the
enemy - tracking several inbound missiles !

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:58.210
Intercept them !

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:23.950
We did it !

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:30.920
In this day and age,
guided weapons are useless.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:33.330
Those rebels,
what are they thinking ?

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:34.920
No...

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:36.130
...this is a feint attack.

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:37.310
What ?

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:38.680
Please take a look at this.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:43.140
The enemy's main force is approaching
from the mining plant to our rear.

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:08.960
Dispatch our
armored vehicle units !

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.350
Looks like we've
made it in time.

00:17:47.970 --> 00:17:49.280
How is it going, Kircheis ?

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:50.900
It'll be done in a minute.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:51.660
Hurry.

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:53.410
I wouldn't want to
let too many soldiers die.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:55.040
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:21.920
Missile cannons #6 and
#8 have been destroyed !

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:25.360
Commander, at this rate...

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:49.720
The program is complete.

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:50.440
Good.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:51.270
Send it.

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:12.370
What just happened ?

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:14.560
There's a incoming
message from Vehicle #52.

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:16.290
Vehicle #52 ?

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.280
It's on the screen.

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:22.160
Ensign Musel...!

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:23.590
Why ?

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.110
Reporting.

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:30.620
During our reconnaissance,
we found an enemy vehicle.

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:33.780
We obtained their computer
data, and analyzed it.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:35.970
Presently, we've sent
a fake command program...

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:39.110
...to the enemy vehicles currently
attacking the base, paralyzing them.

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:42.920
The effect is likely temporary but I ask that you take advantage of this opportunity and defeat them.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:44.460
Wow !

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:49.210
Commander.

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:50.710
Commander.

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:52.230
What is it ?

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:53.460
Please give us your orders.

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:56.490
All vehicles,
destroy the enemy units.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.320
All vehicles,
commence attack !

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:01.300
What's going on ?

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:04.280
Why are they back ?

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:10.510
What happened to Hugenberch ?

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:11.440
He failed ?

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:17.680
That means they know
that I gave the order ?

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:19.430
Or...?

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:22.110
Commander.

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:23.080
Captain.

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:24.750
What is it ?

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:26.680
Our troops are
routing the enemy.

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:28.680
It seems it's only
a matter of time.

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:29.880
I know !

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:34.610
That newly assigned Ensign Musel
has done an excellent job.

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:38.270
And being his first mission, we must
say it's quite an accomplishment.

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:39.440
I know !

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:43.410
Captain, you seem tired.

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:45.100
The outcome is
all but decided.

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:46.810
I don't mean
to be presumptuous...

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:51.020
...but why not leave it to me here
so that you can get some rest ?

00:20:57.170 --> 00:20:58.530
You're right.

00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:00.870
I'll do that.

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:06.500
About Ensign Musel...

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:07.710
Yes ?

00:21:07.710 --> 00:21:11.530
When Ensign Musel returns,
tell him to come to my office.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:14.510
Yes, sir.

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:33.240
How much do they know ?

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:34.780
What...

00:21:34.780 --> 00:21:36.060
...what am I going to do ?

00:22:01.530 --> 00:22:02.340
Yeah !

00:22:02.340 --> 00:22:03.960
We won !

00:22:11.450 --> 00:22:13.120
Just wait for me, Herder...

00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:15.170
...and whoever is behind you...!

00:22:23.090 --> 00:22:28.430
Space Year 791,
Imperial Year 482, July...

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:31.840
...the Imperial Force's B-III base on Planet
Kapche-Lanka suffered much damage...

00:22:31.840 --> 00:22:36.160
...from a Free Planets
Alliance surprise attack.

00:22:36.170 --> 00:22:39.210
But because of the deeds of
Ensign Reinhard von Musel and others...

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:44.470
...they overcame their initial adversity and
succeeded in repelling the enemy attack.

00:22:44.850 --> 00:22:48.300
To be continued

00:22:50.940 --> 00:22:58.560
Reinhard:

00:22:50.940 --> 00:22:58.560
Horikawa Ryo

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:06.610
Herder:

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:06.610
Miyata Hikaru

00:23:06.870 --> 00:23:14.610
Narrator:

00:23:06.870 --> 00:23:14.610
Yara Yuusaku

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:26.100
Pour the light into the night sky, a mystic silver curtain

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:24.810
[ Explanations ]

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:24.810
Ending Theme

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:24.810
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:24.810
Written by: Ogura Kei

00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:30.800
The dance of the entire firmament, the mystery of the aurora

00:23:29.770 --> 00:23:34.750
Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:31.100 --> 00:23:35.460
I believe explanations for those will be given some day

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:40.750
Timing:
Todd Perkins

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:46.700
Even the mystery of this life that it is, some day...

00:23:40.750 --> 00:23:46.760
Song Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:46.760 --> 00:23:52.960
Editing:
Todd Perkins
Barbara
Dave
Brain
Mouse
Jerry
Steve S.
Horus

00:23:47.050 --> 00:23:51.450
...from something to something to be created, to be born -

00:23:51.650 --> 00:23:56.350
Someone will give us an explanation for how that happens

00:23:52.960 --> 00:24:02.920
Subtitled by:
Central Anime(Kansas)

00:23:57.330 --> 00:24:06.500
It is something that intelligent people will figure out

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:11.900
But the answer given to me when I ask "Why ?"...

00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:17.000
...is usually just a formulaic one

00:24:17.280 --> 00:24:22.290
What in the world is that worth ?

00:24:22.450 --> 00:24:29.350
If I ask, they only hesitate to answer

00:24:30.150 --> 00:24:40.150
Why you came to love me isn't something you need to explain

00:24:40.450 --> 00:24:53.050
Those eyes in which the auroras flutter can simply remain a mystery

00:25:10.750 --> 00:25:15.670
